### ============================================================================
### Auth — HRIS Admin & Client API
### ============================================================================
# Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or a compatible .http runner).
#
# Admin auth is served by cmd/admin (internal/bootstrap/admin.go), mounted
# under /api/admin. Client auth is served by cmd/client
# (internal/bootstrap/client.go), mounted under /api — same LoginUserRequest/
# LoginUserResponse payloads, different usecase (AuthUseCase.Login vs
# AuthUseCase.LoginClient) and no client-side /_register.
#
# How to run:
#   1. `make run-admin` (defaults to port 9000, same as config.yml's
#      app.port) and/or `make run-client` — override APP_PORT if running
#      both on this machine at once, they can't share a port.
#   2. Fill in @email / @password below.
#   3. Click "Send Request" on "Login" first. REST Client automatically stores
#      the `token` session cookie and replays it on every request below.
### ============================================================================

@clientBaseUrl = http://localhost:9000/api
@email = admin@company.com
@password = Password123!

### ============================================================================
### Client
### ============================================================================

### Login
# @name clientLogin
POST {{clientBaseUrl}}/_login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

# Note: there is no client-side logout route — only admin registers
# DELETE /users/_logout (auth_router.go, admin package).
